          "guid": "mt3pknyymq131b0m",
          "message": {
            "text": "The outlet's remount-per-route + morph-within-route semantics fall out of kerf's KEYED MORPH for free — no remountOn, no new machinery.\n\noutlet() returns the matched component wrapped in <div data-router-outlet data-key=\"<the matched route's PATTERN>\">. The data-key is the route pattern (/users/:id), not the concrete path:\n- Cross-route navigation (/ → /users/1): the pattern differs → the key differs → kerf's keyed reconcile can't match old-to-new, so it REMOVES the old wrapper and INSERTS the new one = wholesale replacement = fresh DOM. Different pages are never morphed into each other.\n- Same-route param change (/users/1 → /users/2): the pattern is identical → same key → the morph reconciles the wrapper's children in place = the component re-renders with new params, only changed nodes update, scroll/focus preserved.\n\nvoid route.value at the top is the tracked read that subscribes the enclosing mount() to navigation (so the render re-runs); matched is kept in step with the signal in resolve() so the outlet doesn't have to re-match. Verified in tests/unit/router.test.ts › 'renders the matched component, swaps wholesale across routes, updates in place within a route' and the Playwright DOM-identity spec.",
            "markdown": "The outlet's remount-per-route + morph-within-route semantics fall out of kerf's KEYED MORPH for free — no `remountOn`, no new machinery.\n\n`outlet()` returns the matched component wrapped in `<div data-router-outlet data-key=\"<the matched route's PATTERN>\">`. The `data-key` is the route pattern (`/users/:id`), not the concrete path:\n- **Cross-route** navigation (`/` → `/users/1`): the pattern differs → the key differs → kerf's keyed reconcile can't match old-to-new, so it REMOVES the old wrapper and INSERTS the new one = wholesale replacement = fresh DOM. Different pages are never morphed into each other.\n- **Same-route** param change (`/users/1` → `/users/2`): the pattern is identical → same key → the morph reconciles the wrapper's children in place = the component re-renders with new params, only changed nodes update, scroll/focus preserved.\n\n`void route.value` at the top is the tracked read that subscribes the enclosing `mount()` to navigation (so the render re-runs); `matched` is kept in step with the signal in `resolve()` so the outlet doesn't have to re-match. Verified in `tests/unit/router.test.ts` › 'renders the matched component, swaps wholesale across routes, updates in place within a route' and the Playwright DOM-identity spec."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/router.ts"
                },
